# UI Component Standard

Build all new UI from shadcn/ui. The project is configured in `components.json`:
`new-york` style, `zinc` base colour, `lucide` icons, `@@/components/ui` alias.

## Rules

- Compose from `@@/components/ui/*`. Add a missing primitive with
  `npx shadcn@latest add <name>` instead of hand-rolling the markup.
- Do not add `antd`, `@ant-design/icons`, or other component libraries.
- Icons come from `lucide-react`. Decorative icons get `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Style with brand tokens only, never raw hex values in components:
  `bg-primary`, `bg-primary-deep`, `bg-gold`, `text-gold-ink`, `bg-surface`,
  `surface-muted`, `surface-raised`, `text-ink`, `ink-muted`, `ink-subtle`,
  `border-border`, `border-border-muted`, `shadow-card`, `text-link`.
- `gold` (#c89b3c) is only 2.6:1 on white: use it for fills, rules, and accents.
  Use `text-gold-ink` for gold text on light backgrounds (AA 5.3:1).
- Tailwind only scans `src/pages`, `src/components`, and `src/app` (see `tailwind.config.ts`).
  Keep class-string tables under `src/components`, not `src/lib`.
- Page-scoped SCSS lives in `src/styles/pages/<page>.scss` under a page class
  (e.g. `.coming-soon-page`) and is forwarded from `src/styles/globals.scss`.

## Buttons

`variant="default"` for the primary action, `variant="secondary"` for secondary actions,
`variant="outline"` for low-emphasis actions, `variant="ghost"` for icon-only actions.
Use `asChild` with `<a>` / `<Link>` when the button navigates.

## UX / accessibility baseline (WCAG 2.2 AA, Laws of UX)

- One `h1` per page; each `<section>` has one `h2` and `aria-labelledby`.
- One primary CTA per scroll depth.
- Touch targets at least 24x24px (prefer 44px, `min-h-11`).
- Rely on the global `:focus-visible` outline; never remove it without a replacement.
- Animations must respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (handled globally in `base/typography.scss`).
- Meaningful `alt` on informative images; `alt=""` + `aria-hidden` for decorative ones.
- Forms: visible or `sr-only` labels, `aria-invalid` + `aria-describedby` on errors.
